{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/957623-disfigurements","id":957623,"title":"Disfigurements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-25T07:56:49-07:00","id":957623,"title":"Disfigurements","content":"A few questions:<br /> <br /> Is there anything that can cause a Promethean's disfigurements to show for longer than a few seconds (holding on to a subway rail notwithstanding)<br /> Can they choose not to conceal them?<br /> Does Azoth hide Mutations from Flux just as easily as it hides their naturally Disfigured body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:50:20-07:00","id":957828,"title":"","content":"I don't think anything as written can cause them to show long-term, although I could imagine a <i>qashmal</i> Numen that does that, or maybe a Saturninus power. I don't think it would break anything.<br /> <br /> You can't choose to just turn off the Disfigurement-hiding function Azoth permanently, although you can always choose to do Transhuman Potential for 1 turn and show them off for a few seconds.<br /> <br /> I don't think there are rules about the third case, but I'm currently playing a character who used to be Centimani but doesn't have any Dread Powers bought permanently. My approach is that her Disfigurements are visibly weird and mutated and inhuman due to the Flux fallout, but Azoth makes them appear as just normal human things like vitiligo and heterochromia and a palsied hand. I would say that if you bought a third arm or extra eyes or a frog tongue or something, you're gonna want to wear loose clothes because Azoth can't help you. Similar stuff is covered by a Changeling's Mask, but I think in Promethean it's meant to be a bigger deal that you consciously rejected being human to get sick mutant powers, and there are consequences for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}